            <ArticleTitle>Acquired left ventricular to coronary sinus fistula: an unusual complication of acute myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>550-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anatomical complications of myocardial infarction include ventricular septal defect and mitral regurgitation. Another unusual complication of myocardial infarction is described, and its diagnosis and surgical management are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
